# lab.conf.example -- where the lab setup of a machine keeps its tools and ports. Copy it to
# hw/lab.conf (which git ignores; ./x hw bootmode does it when there is none, without these
# header lines) and change what differs on this machine; a key that hw/lab.conf does not set
# takes its value from this file. Read by hw/lab.py (and hw/start_openocd.sh); KEY=value
# lines, no quoting. Another file is named with --lab FILE or the environment variable
# LAB_CONF. The values below are the setup the project was developed on.
#
#   SOFT_CONSOLE  install directory of Microchip SoftConsole. Its OpenOCD has the
#                 microsemi-flashpro interface that the distribution's OpenOCD lacks,
#                 and talks to the embedded FlashPro6 of the Icicle Kit.
#   OCD_HOST      host of the OpenOCD telnet port (the Tcl RPC port is not used: the
#   OCD_PORT      SoftConsole OpenOCD has no read_memory, and md[bhwd] output does
#                 not come back through it)
#   OCD_ROOT      empty if OpenOCD runs on this machine. Else the path of this repository as
#                 OpenOCD sees it (hw/README.md, "OpenOCD on another machine")
#   UART_PATTERN  where the serial port of MMUART <n> is; {n} is the number. Either a device
#                 path (a glob), or a TCP port on another machine where socat tunnels the UART
#                 (see "TCP ports" below): tcp:HOST:PORT or tcp://HOST:PORT. The CP2108 of the
#                 board shows interface if0<n> as MMUART<n>.
#   UART_COUNT    number of serial ports to read (MMUART0 .. MMUART<count-1>)
#   UART<n>       (optional, UART0 .. UART<count-1>) the port of MMUART <n> alone, in the same two
#                 forms; it replaces UART_PATTERN for that MMUART, so device ports and TCP ports
#                 mix. {n} may be used here too.
#   FPGENPROG     the fpgenprog executable of Libero SoC or of the Program Debug Tool: the full path
#                 including the file name (a name on PATH is not enough); hw/bootmode.py runs it. The
#                 other tools of hw/bootmode.py (objcopy, readelf) come from the pinned GNAT cross toolchain
#   FPEXPRESS     the FPExpress executable (FlashPro Express) that hw/program.py runs, and hw/bootmode.py to name the
#                 programmer in the project of fpgenprog: the full path including the file
#                 name. Empty: the FPExpress in the directory of FPGENPROG (the Program Debug Tool and Libero SoC keep
#                 both in one bin directory)
#   TCK_MHZ       JTAG clock in whole MHz (such as 4), for OpenOCD and for FP_Express (hw/program.py).
#                 Empty: both use their own default (OpenOCD 6 MHz; FP_Express 4 MHz or the programming file's).
#   FLASHPRO_TYPE model of the FlashPro that hw/start_openocd.sh starts OpenOCD for: efp6 (embedded FlashPro6),
#                 fp6, efp5 or fp5. Empty: told from the USB product ID (./x hw flashpros shows it)
#   FLASHPRO_ID   the FlashPro as the programming tools of Microchip name it: FP_Express in hw/program.py (--programmer),
#                 fpgenprog in hw/bootmode.py (--flashpro). ./x hw program --scan lists the names with the models. It is not
#                 in general the serial number that OpenOCD and ./x hw flashpros show (S200BM0VJ against 00BM80VJ on one
#                 FlashPro5), and a FlashPro whose USB descriptor has no serial number has only this name. Empty: for a
#                 FlashPro5 that FLASHPRO_SERIAL names, S2 and that serial number (an assumption, checked: hw/program.py looks
#                 for the programmers, and hw/bootmode.py has fpgenprog verify before it programs); else hw/program.py takes
#                 the one FlashPro Express finds, and so does hw/bootmode.py (several: it stops and lists them); without
#                 FlashPro Express bootmode takes FLASHPRO_SERIAL as it is, or the one fpgenprog picks
#   FLASHPRO_SERIAL  serial number of the FlashPro, for a lab with more than one connected (./x hw flashpros lists
#                 them); empty: the one that is found. hw/start_openocd.sh gives it to OpenOCD. hw/bootmode.py takes it for
#                 fpgenprog only when FLASHPRO_ID is empty (with S2 in front for a FlashPro5); for fpgenprog it is not proven
#                 to select (see hw/bootmode.py --help); a run prints the FlashPro used
#   FLASHPRO_USB_LOCATION  USB location of the FlashPro (such as 1-2.3, the name of its directory in
#                 /sys/bus/usb/devices that ./x hw flashpros lists), for one whose USB descriptor has no serial number and
#                 so cannot be chosen by FLASHPRO_SERIAL. hw/start_openocd.sh gives it to OpenOCD as adapter usb location;
#                 whether the driver of the FlashPro honours that was not tried on a board. It changes with the USB port
#   BOOTMODE_DIE  --die of hw/bootmode.py: MPFS250T_ES is the engineering sample that most Icicle Kits carry;
#                 series silicon uses another die name
#   BOOTMODE_PACKAGE  --package of hw/bootmode.py
#
# TCP ports. The board is connected to another machine, and its serial devices are tunnelled from there, one TCP
# port per UART, by socat (run it on that machine; the tools here connect as TCP clients):
#
#   socat TCP-LISTEN:5000,reuseaddr,fork FILE:/dev/serial/by-id/usb-Silicon_Labs_CP2108_...-if00-port0,b115200,raw,echo=0
#
# The baud rate is the one of that socat command (b115200); the tools here cannot set it. {n} is
# replaced by the number as text, so a base port that ends in 0 is "5000 + n" without arithmetic:
# MMUART0 .. MMUART3 on lab-pc, ports 5000 .. 5003:
#
#   UART_PATTERN=tcp://lab-pc:500{n}
#
# Mixed: the devices of this machine, except MMUART2, which is on lab-pc, port 5002:
#
#   UART2=tcp://lab-pc:5002
#
# socat listeners do not authenticate; keep them on a trusted network or reach them through an ssh
# tunnel (ssh -L 5000:localhost:5000 lab-pc, then tcp:localhost:5000), see hw/README.md.
SOFT_CONSOLE=/opt/Microchip_SoftConsole-v2022.2
OCD_HOST=localhost
OCD_PORT=4444
OCD_ROOT=
UART_PATTERN=/dev/serial/by-id/usb-Silicon_Labs_CP2108_*-if0{n}-port0
UART_COUNT=4
FPGENPROG=/opt/Microchip/Libero_SoC/Libero/bin/fpgenprog
FPEXPRESS=
FLASHPRO_ID=
TCK_MHZ=
FLASHPRO_TYPE=
FLASHPRO_SERIAL=
BOOTMODE_DIE=MPFS250T_ES
BOOTMODE_PACKAGE=FCVG484
